# The Open Road

## Verse 1
G                 C
Morning on the highway, engine running low
D                 G
Nothing but the distance and a long way left to go
G                 C
Coffee gone cold, radio on a hum
D                     G
Counting all the mile markers coming one by one

## Chorus
C              G
Take the open road
D              Em
Leave the weight you know
C              G
Wheels beneath the sky
D                    G
No reason and no reason why

## Verse 2
G                 C
Somewhere past the city where the streetlights fade
D                    G
The map runs out of places and the plans we made
G                  C
Windows down, the summer on your face
D                   G
Every town behind us is another empty space

## Chorus
C              G
